WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:05.310 --> 00:00:07.520
So, these are scary times

00:00:07.520 --> 00:00:09.840
but unfortunately there's
more to worry about

00:00:09.840 --> 00:00:11.790
than just a global pandemic.

00:00:11.790 --> 00:00:14.790
New warning from the FBI
about coronavirus scams.

00:00:14.790 --> 00:00:17.100
Scams related to the coronavirus.

00:00:17.100 --> 00:00:19.680
Stealing sensitive personal information.

00:00:19.680 --> 00:00:21.870
It could infect your computer.

00:00:21.870 --> 00:00:23.870
Any time there's a global event,

00:00:23.870 --> 00:00:25.500
hackers like to weaponize it.

00:00:25.500 --> 00:00:28.320
So whether it's the
Olympics or an election

00:00:28.320 --> 00:00:29.800
or a global pandemic,

00:00:29.800 --> 00:00:33.670
hackers are trying to leverage
whatever the situation is

00:00:33.670 --> 00:00:34.620
against users.

00:00:34.620 --> 00:00:36.100
I have an old email address

00:00:36.100 --> 00:00:37.730
with a pretty good spam filter

00:00:37.730 --> 00:00:40.400
and it's just inundated with spam mail

00:00:40.400 --> 00:00:43.620
claiming to be everything from
the World Health Organization

00:00:43.620 --> 00:00:45.750
to COVID-19 vaccines.

00:00:45.750 --> 00:00:47.720
Now I'm not gonna take the bait

00:00:47.720 --> 00:00:48.950
but believe it or not,

00:00:48.950 --> 00:00:50.270
a lot of people will.

00:00:50.270 --> 00:00:52.160
It is working that is why

00:00:52.160 --> 00:00:55.310
hackers and criminal
attackers continue to use it.

00:00:55.310 --> 00:00:56.880
Now I don't need to tell you.

00:00:56.880 --> 00:00:58.550
Well, maybe I should.

00:00:58.550 --> 00:01:00.850
Don't click a link,
don't open attachments.

00:01:00.850 --> 00:01:02.290
Just delete it.

00:01:02.290 --> 00:01:04.960
But for many, that's
easier said than done.

00:01:04.960 --> 00:01:06.810
Phishing emails have quadrupled

00:01:06.810 --> 00:01:08.500
since the coronavirus outbreak.

00:01:08.500 --> 00:01:11.310
It's gotten so bad that
both the U.S. and the U.K.

00:01:11.310 --> 00:01:13.830
Have issued joint warnings
about the schemes.

00:01:13.830 --> 00:01:15.480
So why have all these phishing schemes

00:01:15.480 --> 00:01:18.123
pivoted to coronavirus
practically overnight?

00:01:19.850 --> 00:01:21.710
So a successful phishing campaign,

00:01:21.710 --> 00:01:22.760
it has to be interesting

00:01:22.760 --> 00:01:25.360
and it has to sort of look reliable.

00:01:25.360 --> 00:01:28.020
On one hand, they want
this email to look like

00:01:28.020 --> 00:01:29.490
something you're gonna get anyway

00:01:29.490 --> 00:01:31.840
but they also want it to
grab people's attention

00:01:31.840 --> 00:01:33.550
to say Oh I need to click on this urgently

00:01:33.550 --> 00:01:36.600
and the coronavirus stuff really
fits both of those things.

00:01:36.600 --> 00:01:39.860
People are getting an incredible
amount of email about it

00:01:39.860 --> 00:01:41.990
but it's also a place where
people have a lot of hunger

00:01:41.990 --> 00:01:43.770
for new information.

00:01:43.770 --> 00:01:46.440
But there's one ingredient
that COVID-19 pandemic

00:01:46.440 --> 00:01:50.310
offers hackers that say a
Nigerian prince never could.

00:01:50.310 --> 00:01:51.143
Fear.

00:01:51.143 --> 00:01:52.230
It is scary.

00:01:52.230 --> 00:01:54.182
Millions who are scared right now.

00:01:54.182 --> 00:01:55.800
I am just afraid of this week.

00:01:55.800 --> 00:01:59.100
The idea behind these schemes
is that in times of crisis

00:01:59.100 --> 00:02:01.730
or uncertainty or fear,

00:02:01.730 --> 00:02:03.340
people just let their guards down.

00:02:03.340 --> 00:02:06.380
So in cases where you know
something is promised,

00:02:06.380 --> 00:02:09.280
maybe people are distracted
and not as focused on

00:02:09.280 --> 00:02:10.570
who might be sending something.

00:02:10.570 --> 00:02:13.670
Or in cases where a hacker
is promising information,

00:02:13.670 --> 00:02:15.820
when we're scared, we might
be more likely to click on it

00:02:15.820 --> 00:02:18.440
without thinking twice about
who it might be coming from.

00:02:18.440 --> 00:02:20.910
On top of the fear-based COVID-19 schemes,

00:02:20.910 --> 00:02:23.502
hackers have seized on one of
their tried and true lures,

00:02:23.502 --> 00:02:24.840
money.

00:02:24.840 --> 00:02:27.390
The prospect of a payout
from the two trillion dollars

00:02:27.390 --> 00:02:29.200
stimulus package in the U.S.

00:02:29.200 --> 00:02:31.160
comes with the subject line saying

00:02:31.160 --> 00:02:32.970
COVID-19 payment.

00:02:32.970 --> 00:02:34.690
Again, delete it.

00:02:34.690 --> 00:02:38.020
So it's important to understand
who these hackers are

00:02:38.020 --> 00:02:41.240
and despite all the stock
footage ever made about hackers,

00:02:41.240 --> 00:02:43.853
they're not necessarily
some shady dude in a hoodie.

00:02:45.040 --> 00:02:45.983
These are folks that aren't out

00:02:45.983 --> 00:02:47.930
to sort of make a quick buck.

00:02:47.930 --> 00:02:49.450
Some of these groups can make

00:02:49.450 --> 00:02:51.420
hundreds of millions of dollars in a year

00:02:51.420 --> 00:02:53.300
and sort of have the investments

00:02:53.300 --> 00:02:55.100
to sort of use that money to reinvest

00:02:55.100 --> 00:02:57.080
in sort of grow big capabilities.

00:02:57.080 --> 00:02:58.670
Cybersecurity data suggests

00:02:58.670 --> 00:03:00.640
that many of these hacking operations

00:03:00.640 --> 00:03:03.260
are backed by major nation states.

00:03:03.260 --> 00:03:05.120
So we've seen multiple state-sponsored

00:03:05.120 --> 00:03:07.830
cyber espionage actors who
use coronavirus as a lure.

00:03:07.830 --> 00:03:09.840
We've seen North Korea, China and Russia

00:03:09.840 --> 00:03:12.330
all employ it to try to
compromise their victims.

00:03:12.330 --> 00:03:14.540
And it doesn't stop at spam mail.

00:03:14.540 --> 00:03:17.490
Fake social media accounts
are spreading disinformation

00:03:17.490 --> 00:03:19.810
about the coronavirus
that back the interest

00:03:19.810 --> 00:03:22.200
of countries like China and Russia.

00:03:22.200 --> 00:03:23.980
According to the U.S. State Department,

00:03:23.980 --> 00:03:27.830
Russia has put forth its
entire disinformation apparatus

00:03:27.830 --> 00:03:30.910
to spread disinformation about
the coronavirus pandemic.

00:03:30.910 --> 00:03:34.060
So this includes websites,
conventional media

00:03:34.060 --> 00:03:38.900
and also they stay swarms of
bots on social media platforms

00:03:38.900 --> 00:03:41.610
that are doing the work of amplifying

00:03:41.610 --> 00:03:44.980
or spreading messages that are
false related to the pandemic

00:03:44.980 --> 00:03:48.730
Russia's motivation is to
sow discord and distrust

00:03:48.730 --> 00:03:51.850
and are leveraging the pandemic to create

00:03:51.850 --> 00:03:54.050
a lot of fear and uncertainty

00:03:54.050 --> 00:03:56.150
and make people doubt
healthcare institutions.

00:03:56.150 --> 00:03:58.770
Just because the 2016
election came to an end

00:03:58.770 --> 00:04:02.200
doesn't mean that disinformation campaigns

00:04:02.200 --> 00:04:04.310
from nation state actors
and criminal actors

00:04:04.310 --> 00:04:06.090
didn't come to an end.

00:04:06.090 --> 00:04:09.470
So we are seeing bot nets
from Russia, from Iran,

00:04:09.470 --> 00:04:10.410
from China,

00:04:10.410 --> 00:04:12.080
perfectly willing and capable

00:04:12.080 --> 00:04:14.300
of creating chaos through misinformation.

00:04:14.300 --> 00:04:17.580
And unfortunately, it kind of gets worse

00:04:17.580 --> 00:04:19.720
because hospitals and medical institutions

00:04:19.720 --> 00:04:22.003
are a favorite target for hackers.

00:04:23.590 --> 00:04:27.360
What they will do is hit
a target with ransomware

00:04:27.360 --> 00:04:29.820
which is an attack that uses malware

00:04:29.820 --> 00:04:34.260
to encrypt or lock down data
belonging to an organization.

00:04:34.260 --> 00:04:37.640
And they'll charge a ransom for
the decryption of that data.

00:04:37.640 --> 00:04:40.130
And from a criminal perspective,

00:04:40.130 --> 00:04:42.660
those attacks might be more successful

00:04:42.660 --> 00:04:45.540
during a time when healthcare
institutions are so important.

00:04:45.540 --> 00:04:49.210
There is increased targeting
on medical facilities,

00:04:49.210 --> 00:04:53.050
hospitals, testing centers,
primary care physicians

00:04:53.050 --> 00:04:55.960
because they are so dire, so desperate

00:04:55.960 --> 00:04:57.510
to keep their operations up.

00:04:57.510 --> 00:05:00.173
If they shut down, there
are lives at stake.

00:05:03.070 --> 00:05:04.550
Just as we must band together

00:05:04.550 --> 00:05:06.850
to defeat the COVID-19 pandemic,

00:05:06.850 --> 00:05:09.930
we must also be vigilant
against the people and nations

00:05:09.930 --> 00:05:13.590
shamelessly trying to capitalize
on these trying times.

00:05:13.590 --> 00:05:16.740
In terms of disinformation campaigns,

00:05:16.740 --> 00:05:18.020
it's important to think about

00:05:18.020 --> 00:05:20.170
who you're receiving information from,

00:05:20.170 --> 00:05:24.750
trusting official
sources and not believing

00:05:24.750 --> 00:05:28.040
everything that's on social
media about the pandemic.

00:05:28.040 --> 00:05:30.590
Instead, going to trusted news outlets.

00:05:30.590 --> 00:05:32.830
Always be on the lookout to communication

00:05:32.830 --> 00:05:34.430
that you don't normally get.

00:05:34.430 --> 00:05:36.440
Sort of the ways to check
that you can double check

00:05:36.440 --> 00:05:38.330
who the sender is from,

00:05:38.330 --> 00:05:40.810
making sure they're exactly
sort of who you're expecting.

00:05:40.810 --> 00:05:42.330
Just opening and looking at an email

00:05:42.330 --> 00:05:44.450
in your Gmail browser is

00:05:44.450 --> 00:05:46.360
it's gonna be very unlikely to infect you.

00:05:46.360 --> 00:05:49.180
But your risk increases a lot
when you open an attachment

00:05:49.180 --> 00:05:50.420
or click on a link.

00:05:50.420 --> 00:05:52.630
So you can generally
read an email and be okay

00:05:52.630 --> 00:05:54.360
but be very wary of attachments or links

00:05:54.360 --> 00:05:56.500
especially if they're unexpected.

00:05:56.500 --> 00:05:59.150
So while we all understand
the temptation to click,

00:05:59.150 --> 00:06:01.540
out of fear or even greed,

00:06:01.540 --> 00:06:04.423
please do yourself a
favor and just delete it.

